Z||000004||terryk||01-15-2001||12:21 AM||||Yes it fits and several people have done the swap.||||reg||1
Z||000005||lowCG||01-15-2001||12:30 AM||||I drive mine daily with the swapped in 3.4TDC,and I too was being realistic about trying not to over-spend on a car that'll probably not re-sell for much;figure I spent around $2600 for a 30K '97 Monte motor with the stainless exhaust,real-time fuel mixture controller factored in.<BR>I'm sure it could be done cheaper,but I'm having no regrets <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||01-15-2001||01:44 AM||||LowCg, how did you handle the dogbone? The old strut to the PS mount?||||reg||5
Z||000007||DreXteR||01-15-2001||09:09 AM||||Lowcg,  in order to make the swap, the starter have to be relocated?<BR>And please list all the process involved in this swap.<P>Thanx<P>DerXteR||||reg||5
Z||000008||lowCG||01-15-2001||09:06 PM||||Terry,I used Chris West's urethane mounts,so I'm boneless,the ears were ground off smooth and painted.I remember also re-sculpting the ear next to the PS bracket also.<BR>The swap was pretty much grinding off several things in and around the engine compartment;making a spacer to move the clutch slave/shifter cable away from the exhaust crossover pipe;making a new hole in the firewall towards the driver's side,plugging the one left towards the passenger's side to route one of the shifter cables through;bolting on Chris West's urethane motor mounts;making a new end on the Fiero throttle cable to be able and attach to the new throttle body;re-route fuel lines over towards the driver's side of the compartment;make a custom exhaust;sort out the wires going to and from the ECM,fuel pump,ignition,speedo,and replace the load that the automatic had on the shifter solenoid circuits(3)with some pretty large resistors.<BR>The intake can be routed directly to the stock air filter setup until you hear how it sounds without a baffle,then you make a large,open,loud intake.<BR>I also used a fuel controller from Split Second that I use to fine tune the idle,midrange,top end,and accelleration.||||reg||1
Z||000009||terryk||01-15-2001||09:53 PM||||Thanks for the info LowCG. The engine is in and running nicely but I think a dogbone is a must. We've been toying with some options. One is a strut bar with a mount on it. The engine's in an 85GT. The engine has a custom Y-pipe down to a 2-1/2" system that follows the stock routing. We used a front manifold in the back so it would allow the Y-pipe. The ECM is a stock 9396 using manual trans code, but I had to change a few things in the code to get the speedo to read correctly. That was fun. The speedo would peg and the ECM would read 0. You could put 1 mile on the odo just backing out of the driveway! Finally got that squared away. <P>Thanks again!<P>Terry<BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 01-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||DreXteR||01-16-2001||12:20 AM||||Thanx for the info.  U have a web page with the prosess?<P>Thanx||||reg||1
Z||000011||terryk||01-16-2001||01:06 AM||||I don't, no. Billions of pics out there already.||||reg||1
Z||000012||lowCG||01-16-2001||09:41 PM||||No,but once the engines out of the car,and the new one's waiting to go in,you just take one issue at a time until it's all ready to go into the car.The wiring was the most intensive part,taking the better part of a week of evenings,and a weekend to sort it all out.||||reg||1
Z||000013||lowCG||01-16-2001||09:42 PM||||No website,but once the engines out of the car,and the new one's waiting to go in,you just take one issue at a time until it's all ready to go into the car.The wiring was the most intensive part,taking the better part of a week of evenings,and a weekend to sort it all out.I started with a long list,and kept at it until it was time to turn the key.||||reg||1
Z||000014||DreXteR||01-16-2001||11:38 PM||||Where I can find any performance part for 3.4 TDC?<P>Thanx <P><BR>DreX||||reg||5
Z||000015||Dan86gt3.8||01-17-2001||11:21 AM||||Low cg, what did you do for a better intake?  I am running the stock setup on mine.  Are thier baffles through the stock setup?  Does it just make a sound difference or does it increase power?<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>1/4- 15.3@90mph||||reg||1
Z||000016||lowCG||01-17-2001||07:42 PM||||I pretty much chose that engine because I wouldn't be needing funky aftermarket parts,I don't really like the stuff unless it's on a duece coupe,racecar or something,just not worth the hassles.<BR>The intake is just two Fiero K&Ns in the driver's rear fenderwell,connected by a 4" duct,and some PVC parts,all coupled together with rubber sleeves/clamps.I've made a louvered panel to go under the opening to keep water out from the rear tire/road,it attaches to the subframe,also,I've partially closed off the intake scoop to keep rain out as well.<BR>The performance did increase a little over a K&N in the stock canister,but the sound is what's truly incredible!||||reg||1
